# --- s063 Book I d.25 q. un. (pp. 99–101)
n("n1144","s063-01","persona ita est ad se sicut deus","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VII 6.11: *non enim aliud est Deo esse, aliud personam esse* (checked locally).","verified")
n("n1145","s063-01","trinitas diuina est personarum inuicem relatiuarum","la","source","A paraphrase of Augustine, *De Trin.* V–VII (the persons are said relatively to one another); the exact wording has not been located.","to-verify")
n("n1146","s063-02","Confirmatur per Aug. 7. de trini.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VII (see n1145).","to-verify")
n("n1147","s063-04","et aliqua persona sit absoluta vt potentia","la","textual","B: *cum ens diuidatur … et aliqua sint absoluta vt potentia*. B gives better sense: *being* is divided into absolute and relative, and the absolute example (power) is not a person. A’s *persona* is probably a compositor’s anticipation, and A also lacks *ens*. The translation follows B. B checked.","probable")
n("n1148","s063-04","Thomas anglicus","la","historical","An English Thomas, presumably a Dominican (Thomas Sutton?) or Thomas Wylton; possibly Thomas Jorz (*Thomas Anglicus*). Not identified. B: *Tho. anglicus* (= A). B checked.","uncertain")
n("n1149","s063-05","per alium modum a primis","la","source","This second series follows Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 25 q. un. closely (Wadding text checked locally): ‘person’ is not a proper relation (it is common); it is not a common relation (the *duplum/multiplex* argument); it is not the substance (which is not numbered); and the two views, that ‘person’ is a double negation connoting the persons, the relations and the essence, or that it is something positive and abstracting.","verified")
n("n1150","s063-05","Si sunt inquit tres persone: commune est eis hoc quod est persona","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VII 4.7: *Si enim tres Personae, commune est eis id quod persona est* (checked locally). Gorris’s *c. 7* is his chapter division.","verified")
n("n1151","s063-05","duplum dimidium","la","textual","A *dimidium*; B *duplum dimidij*, which the sense requires (cf. *multiplex dimidii* following). The translation follows B. B checked.","certain")
n("n1152","s063-05","Et hec est opinio Scoti","la","doctrinal","Cf. *Ord.* I d. 25 q. un.: Scotus sets out both views without condemning the first.","probable")
n("n1153","s063-04","some things are absolute, as power","en","translation","The translation follows B (*cum ens diuidatur … et aliqua sint absoluta*). A reads ‘and some person is absolute, as power’.")
n("n1154","s063-05","namely to the half","en","translation","The translation follows B *dimidij*; A has *dimidium*.")
